gstudio 1.15.0 - 20261007
-----------------
* [BREAKING] (1.15.0) This release marks the interface changes below; they break code written for 1.14 (installed from GitHub) and have no deprecation period.
* [BREAKING] (1.15.0) Removed exports: A(), Ae(), He(), Hes(), Hi(), Ho(), Hos(), Ht(), Fis() and Pe() (use genetic_diversity(mode = ...)); Fst(), Gst(), Gst_prime() and Dest() (use genetic_structure(mode = ...)); dist_amova(), dist_bray(), dist_cavalli(), dist_cgd(), dist_euclidean(), dist_jaccard(), dist_nei() and dist_ss() (use genetic_distance(mode = ...)); rel_lynch(), rel_nason(), rel_queller() and rel_ritland() (use genetic_relatedness(mode = ...)); to_SpatialPoints() and to_SpatialLines() (use to_sf()).
* [BREAKING] (1.15.0) hwe() columns Chi and Prob are now statistic and p.value, and p.value is numeric (Prob was a character string).
* [BREAKING] (1.15.0) genetic_structure() column P is now p.value; with nperm > 0 the Multilocus row is now tested too.
* [BREAKING] (1.15.0) genetic_autocorrelation() column P is now p.value.
* [BREAKING] (1.15.0) optimal_sampling() columns Strata, Var.Phi, Var.Phi.Low and Var.Phi.High are now Stratum, var_phi, conf.low and conf.high.
* [BREAKING] (1.15.0) asymmetric_weights() columns i and j are now from and to.
* [BREAKING] (1.15.0) to_df() node tables name the node column Stratum (was name) and edge tables use from and to (were From and To).
* [BREAKING] (1.15.0) centroid_variance() returns a data.frame with columns Stratum and variance (was a named vector).
* [BREAKING] (1.15.0) plot() on a popgraph returns a ggplot (was igraph base graphics; igraph::plot.igraph() is still available).
* [CHANGE] (1.15.0) genetic_diversity() gains modes Hi (per-individual heterozygosity) and Ht (Nei's total heterozygosity), so every diversity estimator is reachable from it; mode = can take several values (e.g. c("A", "Ae", "He")) and returns one table with a column for each; loci= is now honoured when a stratum is given; Hes, Hos and Ht give a clear error without a stratum.
* [CHANGE] (1.15.0) Output columns follow one convention: populations keyed by 'Stratum', edges by 'from'/'to', and tables of tests use broom::tidy() names (statistic, df, p.value, conf.low/conf.high).  See the [BREAKING] entries above for the renamed columns.  source_sink_scores() and gravity_field() (new in this release) key populations by 'Stratum' (was 'node' during development).
* [FIX] (1.15.0) hwe() returns numeric p-values (they were formatted as character strings).
* [ADD] (1.15.0) genetic_structure(nperm = ) now tests the Multilocus row of Gst, Gst' and Dest by permuting strata across individuals (shared by all loci); it was always NA.
* [CHANGE] (1.15.0) Tests return standard 'htest' objects (print like t.test(), work with broom::tidy()): source_sink_test() (statistic r, two-sided p, nodes/nperm, degree share as estimate; scores and the null kept as extra fields), directional_test() (V or forward-edge count, median deviation; the per-edge table moves to $edges), and asymmetry_network() / asymmetry_significance(mode = "existence") (observed mean |Delta| against the rewiring null).
* [CHANGE] (1.15.0) Per-edge result tables use broom::tidy() column names: asymmetry_significance(mode = "location"/"mechanism"), asymmetry_permutation() and asymmetry_bandwidth() report p.value (was p_value); asymmetry_ci() reports conf.low / conf.high (was ci_low / ci_high).
* [CHANGE] (1.15.0) Grouped data frames supply the stratum: when 'stratum' is not given, the group_by() variable is used by genetic_diversity(), genetic_structure(), genetic_distance(), frequencies(), frequency_matrix(), genotype_counts(), allele_counts(), population_graph(), strata_coordinates() and partition(); an explicit 'stratum' (even one equal to the default) always wins.
* [FIX] (1.15.0) population_graph() and the other functions above accept tibbles (population_graph() previously failed with "invalid 'times' argument"); genetic_distance() and population_graph() no longer fail on grouped data, and strata_coordinates() no longer ignores the grouping.
* [FIX] (1.15.0) make_population() / make_populations() select the Locus, Allele and Frequency columns by name. They were taken by position, so a frequency table with columns in another order (e.g. from expand.grid()) failed or silently used the wrong columns.
* [ADD] (1.15.0) genetic_distance(mode = "pgd"): partitioned conditional genetic distance among strata, i.e. each Population Graph edge's cGD split into directed shares by the genetic-gravity neighbourhood weights and returned as all-pairs directed shortest-path distances (asymmetric; [i, j] is the distance from i to j, shorter in the direction of gene flow). The bandwidth is passed as genetic_distance(..., gamma = 0.5); other modes report unused arguments.
* [ADD] (1.15.0) plot.popgraph(): plot() on a Population Graph now returns a ggplot (previously it fell through to igraph's base-graphics plot.igraph(), still available as igraph::plot.igraph()). Nodes are placed from Longitude/Latitude (or x/y) vertex attributes when present, otherwise with a seeded Kamada-Kawai layout (better node separation than Fruchterman-Reingold), sized by the vertex 'size' attribute (for popgraph() graphs, within-population genetic variability), falling back to degree when the graph has none, and coloured by a 'region' vertex attribute (any capitalisation) when present; options layout, node_size, node_labels, node_fill (NULL for that default, a colour, or the name of a categorical or continuous vertex attribute), edges, edge_width and base. Nodes are drawn as a dot under a black ring, and a mapped node_fill uses the colour scale (restyle with scale_colour_*()), leaving the fill scale free for underlays such as the gravity surface. Directed graphs (asymmetric_popgraph()) are drawn with arrows, reciprocal arcs offset side by side.
* [CHANGE] (1.15.0) One plotting backend for plot.popgraph(), plot.gravity_field(), plot.gravity_congruence() and animate_popgraphs(), so their shared options behave identically. Named layouts use edge weights floored at a quarter of their median and a fixed seed (reproducible without set.seed(), leaving the caller's RNG state untouched). Plot options must be named and come after '...'; a mistyped or unsupported option (e.g. plot(field, gamma = 1)) is reported by chkDots() instead of being silently ignored.
* [CHANGE] (1.15.0) gravity_field(graph, gamma) is now analysis only and the single entry point for multi-panel fields: it accepts a graph, a named list of graphs, or one graph with several gamma values (one panel each). Coordinates moved to plot(field, layout = ...); the coords/layout arguments, the x/y/x_mid/y_mid/ux/uy columns and coords_source are gone. Tables gain a 'panel' column, diagnostics is a per-panel data.frame (with gamma), the input graphs are kept in $graphs, as.data.frame() gains what = "diagnostics", and c() combines fields into one multi-panel field. When all panels share their populations they are drawn on one layout. The default layout (shared with plot.popgraph()) remains "kk".
* [CHANGE] (1.15.0) plot_gravity_field() is no longer exported; use plot() on a gravity_field. Display options (surface, arrows, palette, mask_dist, arrow_scale, min_delta, grid_n, subtitle_stats) are unchanged.
* [ADD] (1.15.0) gravity_congruence(x, y, gamma = 0.5, nperm = 999): do two species (or markers, or censuses) move genes the same way across the same populations? Each graph's gravity is computed on its own full topology and compared at two levels, reported in a broom-style $tests table (test, statistic, parameter, p.value, nperm, method, alternative): source-sink scores by Spearman rho(S1, S2) with a population-label permutation test, and edge direction as the proportion of shared edges whose Delta has the same sign in both graphs, with an exact binomial (sign) test against 1/2 conditional on the shared edges. $nodes gives S.1/S.2, gravity, degree and a concordance class (shared source, shared sink, discordant), $edges the shared edges with weight.1/.2, delta.1/.2 and concordant, and $graphs the decorated congruence topology plus both input graphs. Requires exactly the same population set; accepts graphs or single-panel gravity fields. print(), as.data.frame(what = c("nodes", "edges", "tests")) and plot() methods; plot() maps the shared source-sink score (red where both graphs agree on a source, blue on a sink, white where they disagree), arrows on concordant edges and dashes on discordant ones (with a "Shared edges" legend), and colours nodes by concordance.
* [ADD] (1.15.0) population_graph(decorate = TRUE) averages every numeric, non-locus column within each stratum and adds it as a vertex attribute, so Latitude/Longitude become each node's barycenter and plot(), to_sf() and ibgd() pick up the coordinates directly. Columns named name or size are skipped. Default FALSE, so existing code (e.g. simulations) gets the same graphs as before.
* [ADD] (1.15.0) gravity_field() carries the graph's decorations: $nodes and $edges gain every other vertex and edge attribute after the computed columns (computed columns win on a name clash; panels missing an attribute get NA), and the graphs in $graphs keep all their attributes and gain S and gravity vertex attributes and a delta edge attribute (oriented as igraph::ends()).
* [ADD] (1.15.0) congruence_topology() carries the parents' vertex attributes onto the congruence topology: an attribute in one graph is copied, one with equal values in both is copied once, and one that differs (e.g. size) is kept as <name>.1 and <name>.2.
* [ADD] (1.15.0) ibgd() uses the great-circle distance (km, via strata_distance()) between nodes when x and distance are both NULL and the graph has Longitude and Latitude vertex attributes; mode = "pgd" still needs forward.
* [ADD] (1.15.0) plot.gravity_field(): node_fill now works as for plot.popgraph() (default NULL, a colour, or any vertex attribute of the field's graphs, including S and gravity); node colours and the source-sink surface get separate legends. New alpha = sets the surface's opacity (0-1), also on plot.gravity_congruence().
* [ADD] (1.15.0) base = on plot() for popgraphs, gravity fields and gravity congruences, and on animate_popgraphs(): a ggplot to draw the graph on, so layers can go underneath it (e.g. a map: plot(graph, base = ggplot() + geom_polygon(...) + coord_sf(...))). The graph's layers do not inherit the base plot's mappings, and the base's coordinate system, theme and axis labels are kept.
* [FIX] (1.15.0) ibgd() reports the graph's name in data.name; it printed the whole deparsed graph.
* [CHANGE] (1.15.0) animate_popgraphs(): default frames are drawn with the shared backend (ggraph is now only needed for a custom frame_plot); 'labels = TRUE/FALSE' is replaced by node_labels, and node_size and node_fill are added; layout defaults to NULL (vertex coordinates when every node has them, otherwise "kk").
* [CHANGE] (1.15.0) source_sink_test(): near-ties in S are merged by tolerance (sorted values within 1e-10 * max|S| of their neighbour share one value) instead of rounding to 12 significant digits, which failed to merge true ties that straddle a rounding boundary (two leaves differing by 4.6e-16). interior = TRUE now keeps nodes at least edge_margin from either end of x (was more than), so the default edge_margin = 2 trims two demes at each end; code that used edge_margin = 1 to get demes 3-23 of 1-25 should now use the default. Results are otherwise unchanged.
* [CHANGE] (1.15.0) asymmetric_weights() / asymmetric_popgraph(): the perplexity search caps the target at k - tol for a node with k neighbours (k is the largest perplexity it can reach) and brackets sigma from the data, [max(1e-6, min d / 100), max(10, 10 max d)], instead of the fixed [1e-6, 10]. Weights change for nodes with fewer neighbours than 'perplexity' and for edge weights outside the old bracket.
* [FIX] (1.15.0) asymmetric_weights() / asymmetric_popgraph() no longer fail with "missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed". A node with more near-equal neighbour distances than 'perplexity' drove sigma down until every kernel term underflowed (0/0); the kernel now subtracts the smallest exponent first, which leaves the normalised weights unchanged (to ~1e-15) where they were already finite.
* [ADD] (1.15.0) return_null = TRUE on asymmetry_network(), asymmetry_permutation(), asymmetry_bandwidth() and asymmetry_significance() keeps the null distribution: $null_distribution (valid rewired graphs' mean |Delta|) on the existence htest, attribute "null_distribution" (edges x permutations, rows aligned with the returned edges, also after pendants = "drop") on the per-edge tables.
* [FIX] (1.15.0) Corrected the Dyer & Nason (2004) Population Graphs citation in ?genetic_gravity, ?asymmetry_significance and ?graph_asymmetries to Molecular Ecology 13: 1713-1727.
* [FIX] (1.15.0) The "kk" layout for gravity fields (now plot(field, layout = "kk")) floors the pGD arc weights at a quarter of their median before Kamada-Kawai, as the "fr" layout already did. Near-zero arcs had collapsed groups of nodes onto the same point, which masked almost the whole surface and produced "Zero contours were generated" and min/max warnings.
* [FIX] (1.15.0) plot() on a gravity field floors the nearest-neighbour scale used for mask_dist and the interpolation bandwidth at a quarter of the nodes' mean spacing, so near-coincident coordinates cannot blank the surface.
* [CHANGE] Unified Core API: Consolidated all distance, relatedness, and differentiation estimators under three canonical front-ends: genetic_distance(), genetic_relatedness(), and genetic_structure(). Individual dist_*(), rel_*(), and Fst()/Gst() functions are now internal.
* [CHANGE] Modernized Dependencies: Fully removed deprecated 'sp' dependency in favor of 'sf'. Replaced 'reshape2' and 'stringi' with base R equivalents (stats::xtabs, iconv).
* [CHANGE] Standardized S3 Class Order: Graph constructors now consistently set class(graph) <- c("popgraph", "igraph") to ensure popgraph method dispatch precedence.
* [ADD] Native Tidyverse Support: Added automatic stratum detection (.detect_stratum) so piped dplyr::group_by() workflows work seamlessly across frequencies(), genetic_diversity(), genetic_structure(), and all differentiation statistics.
* [ADD] Documentation: Added working @examples to all public functions (using \dontrun{} for file I/O operations).
* [PERF] Vectorization: Major performance optimizations in is.na.locus() (>900x speedup), dist_amova() (~100x speedup), cov2dist(), and column_class().
* [FIX] Mathematical Corrections: Corrected permutation locus alignment in Fst(); eliminated silent column recycling in Gst()/Dest(); resolved stratum misordering in Fis(); fixed Gower centering in distance_to_covariance(); corrected shared allele distance direction in dist_bray(); fixed weighting and calculation in relatedness estimators (LynchRitland, Ritland, Nason); and handled missing data edge cases safely across paternity(), migrate(), and mate().
* [TEST] Added >240 new unit test assertions, raising overall package test coverage to 85.4% across 1,134 passing tests.
* [ADD] Genetic gravity: neighbourhood_weights(), gravity_edges() and source_sink_scores() return the neighbourhood-weight matrix w_{j|i}, the edge asymmetry Delta_{i->j} = w_{i|j} - w_{j|i} (positive when i is the source) with its degree-only term Delta0 = 1/k_j - 1/k_i, and each population's gravity, source-sink balance and least-squares source-sink score S (S_i - S_j ~ Delta_{i->j}, centred within each connected component). One sign convention throughout: higher = more of a source. The bandwidth is b_i = gamma * s_i/k_i, default gamma = 0.5 (degree-neutral, for inferring direction); gamma = 1 is the local mean (for describing connectivity) and gamma = Inf the flat, degree-only kernel. source_sink_scores() attaches the degree diagnostics to report with any directional analysis (degree_share = R^2 of Delta on Delta0, cor(S, S0), cor(S, degree), gradient_share) and, given a covariate x, each node's orientation imbalance and the decomposition of the axis-oriented sum |E| Delta-bar. Validated against the Genetic Gravity manuscript code to 1e-15.
* [ADD] source_sink_test(): Spearman r(S, x) between source-sink scores and a hypothesized covariate, with a Moran spectral randomization null on the graph's own topology (default; kernel-weighted adjacency exp(-e^2 / 2 bbar^2)), plain permutation, or spectral randomization on a user-supplied adjacency; two-sided p, optional interior-only statistic (interior = TRUE drops leaves and edge_margin units of x at each end; the default 2 keeps demes 3-23 of 1-25), S values within 1e-10 * max|S| treated as tied before ranking so floating-point near-ties cannot change ranks. Reproduces the manuscript's p-values exactly for a given seed.
* [ADD] msr_null(): native Moran spectral randomization ("singleton" method of Wagner & Dray 2015), a port of adespatial::msr() with spdep::mat2listw(style = "B") weights; same replicates as adespatial for a given seed, without depending on adespatial or spdep.
* [ADD] pgd() (partitioned conditional genetic distance, as a directed graph or all-pairs directed distance matrix) and ibgd(graph, x, mode = c("cgd", "pgd")), isolation by graph distance returned as an 'htest': mode = "cgd" tests cor(cGD, separation) with a Mantel permutation test (one-sided, nperm = 999); mode = "pgd" fits directed pGD with forward and reverse slopes and reports Delta R^2 = adj R^2_pGD - R^2_cGD with the R^2s, slopes and forward-to-reverse slope ratio (no p-value: the fits are not nested). Accepts a 1-D position or a distance matrix with an orientation matrix.
* [ADD] gravity_field() and plot_gravity_field(). gravity_field() returns an S3 object of class "gravity_field": node coordinates (matrix, strata_coordinates() output, vertex attributes, or a seeded layout), source-sink scores, source-to-sink edge vectors, gamma, the degree diagnostics and the coordinate source, with print(), plot() and as.data.frame(what = c("nodes", "edges")) methods. plot_gravity_field() draws a ggplot "wind map" from graphs, precomputed fields, or a list mixing them: inverse-distance-weighted (or nearest-node) source-sink surface with contours, grey edges, midpoint arrows scaled by |Delta|, nodes sized by degree, degree share and cor(S, degree) in the facet labels; several graphs or fields (or one graph at several gamma) are faceted on common colour and arrow scales. Base R and ggplot2 only.
* [ADD] locus_subsample_null(): rebuilds the Population Graph from random subsets of polymorphic loci and records mean |Delta| with the polymorphism of the loci used, as an information-loss reference for the asymmetry index.
* [ADD] migration_matrix(model = "stepping_stone_1d_asym", m_fwd, m_rev): a directional 1-D stepping stone (rates to the higher- and lower-indexed neighbour, not split between neighbours), for simulate_pop() studies of directional gene flow.
* [ADD] graph_asymmetries() gains gamma (an alias for scale) and accepts scale = Inf (flat kernel, w = 1/k). If the Gaussian kernel underflows at very small bandwidths it now falls back to a log-sum-exp evaluation instead of returning NaN; otherwise its output is unchanged (bit-identical, Swift parity tests pass).
* [ADD] Population Graphs vignette section "Genetic Gravity" (choosing the bandwidth, scores, mapping, the source-sink test, directional IBGD, information loss, simulating directional gene flow), and 45 unit test assertions for the gravity functions (weights sum to one, gravity balances, S reproduces Delta on trees, scale invariance, flat-kernel degree share = 1, component centring, msr moments, mirror symmetry of the test, pGD partition, arrow direction, common plot scales).
* [ADD] Example data 'gravity': raw genotypes (2,500 individuals, 25 populations, 20 biallelic loci) from one census of the Genetic Gravity manuscript simulations, a 25-deme stepping stone with gene flow biased 4:1 toward higher-numbered populations (Redistributed scenario, lineage 4, generation 2504), chosen as the plateau-core census with the strongest source-sink gradient detected by both tests. Population Graphs are built from it with popgraph(to_mv(gravity), gravity$Population). The framework help page for neighbourhood_weights(), gravity_edges() and source_sink_scores() is now ?genetic_gravity.
* [ADD] Vignette 'genetic_gravity': the model in brief, then a worked analysis from the gravity genotypes to a Population Graph, neighbourhood weights, edge asymmetries, source-sink scores, bandwidth choice and degree diagnostics, the source-sink gradient test, directional isolation by graph distance with pGD, and the gravity field map.
* [CHANGE] Removed the commented-out as.data.frame.genind() and its stale @importFrom adegenet roxygen tags, so regenerating the documentation can no longer add adegenet to NAMESPACE; gstudio has no adegenet, adespatial or spdep dependency.

gstudio 1.14.1 - 1.14.5 - 20260610
-----------------
* [FIX] (1.14.5) asymmetry_significance(mode = "location") / asymmetry_permutation() now centre the two-tailed test on each edge's permutation null mean, |null - mean(null)| >= |obs - mean(null)|, instead of on zero. With a fixed topology each edge's null is shifted by its degree component (roughly 1/k_i - 1/k_j), so the old |Delta| comparison sent observed values lying between zero and that centre to p ~ 1. The 'statistic' column now reports the centred deviation Delta_obs - mean(null); 'delta' is unchanged.
* [FIX] (1.14.5) randomize_graph(mode = "degree") now uses igraph::rewire(keeping_degseq()) edge swaps. The previous whole-configuration rejection sampler failed on dense graphs (above ~80 edges on 25 nodes), missed reversed duplicate pairs and so could return multi-edges, and reported the wrong iteration limit. Rewired graphs are always simple, preserve every node's degree, and keep the original vertex order. This changes the null draws of asymmetry_network() / mode = "existence", which no longer fails on dense graphs.
* [CHANGE] (1.14.5) asymmetry_network() only suggests rewire = "degree" in its no-valid-draws error when rewire = "full" was used.
* [ADD] (1.14.4) Added animate_popgraphs() to render a list of population graphs as an animated GIF with a fixed node layout (default Fruchterman-Reingold on the union graph; user may supply a layout name, layout function, coordinate matrix, or strata_coordinates() output) and a user-set frame delay. Uses the 'gifski' package (Suggests).
* [ADD] Added asymmetry_significance() wrapper for testing the significance of the edge asymmetry index, with mode = c("permutation","jackknife","bandwidth","network") dispatching to new base functions asymmetry_permutation() (fixed-topology label permutation), asymmetry_jackknife() (within-stratum bootstrap stability CIs), asymmetry_bandwidth() (bandwidth-alignment permutation), and asymmetry_network() (rewiring null). Returns a tidy per-edge data.frame.
* [CHANGE] (1.14.4) Reorganised asymmetry_significance() as a hierarchy of successively conditioned permutation tests, with mode = c("existence","location","mechanism") replacing the earlier mode names ("network","permutation","bandwidth"). Each mode is now documented by the ecological/evolutionary hypothesis it tests and what failing to reject it implies. Results no longer carry the always-NA ci_low/ci_high columns, and the three base functions asymmetry_network(), asymmetry_permutation(), and asymmetry_bandwidth() return the same five columns.
* [ADD] (1.14.4) Added asymmetry_ci(), a within-stratum bootstrap confidence interval on each edge's asymmetry index for reporting its magnitude (e.g. Delta = X, 95% CI: low-high). Returns an edge_support column giving the proportion of resamples in which the edge was re-estimated, since the interval is conditional on the edge being present. Replaces asymmetry_jackknife() and the former "support"/"jackknife" mode of asymmetry_significance(); this is an estimate, not a hypothesis test, so it is no longer offered as a significance mode.
* [FIX] (1.14.4) Bootstrap resampling of a stratum containing a single individual now resamples that individual rather than drawing from 1:n (base R sample() gotcha).
* [FIX] (1.14.4) asymmetry_significance(mode = "location") / asymmetry_permutation() no longer fail when 'alpha' is passed; it is ignored with a warning since the fixed-topology test requires alpha = 1. Failed permutations are dropped from the null rather than aborting.
* [FIX] (1.14.4) asymmetry_ci() excludes bootstrap resamples that fail to produce a graph from edge_support and the intervals (previously counted as "edge absent"), warns about them, and records the count in attr(x, "nboot_failed").
* [FIX] (1.14.4) asymmetry_network() / mode = "existence" records rewired graphs with isolated nodes as NA instead of aborting.
* [FIX] (1.14.4) asymmetry_ci() and mode = "location" now error when 'groups' does not contain every graph node, instead of returning all-NA results.
* [CHANGE] (1.14.4) asymmetry_significance() warns when 'data'/'groups' are supplied to a mode that ignores them.
* [CHANGE] (1.14.4) animate_popgraphs() now writes to a temporary file by default (CRAN policy), draws frames with ggraph, and accepts a frame_plot = function(layout, title) for custom ggraph styling. Requires 'ggraph' (Suggests).
* [FIX] (1.14.4) Vectorized `+` and `-` on locus vectors now recycle a length-one operand, error on mismatched lengths, and (for `+`) return NA for missing genotypes with a warning instead of stopping.
* [FIX] (1.14.4) to_fixed_locus() formats locus vectors element-wise instead of concatenating them into one string.
* [CHANGE] (1.14.4) column_class() returns character(0)/integer(0) instead of NA when no column matches; internal callers updated.

